-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the bridge from codes (unverified)
-- a code that is an application of globals to variables and other such codes reads as a term:
-- a global is a constant (by its index), a variable a variable, an application an application;
-- anything else is outside the fragment. The equations the store holds (lib/rules.cub reads them
-- as rules) are hypotheses of this form once their Π binders are peeled; the goal, a code, is
-- read the same way, and what check-eq accepts about the terms eq-cert-sound proves about them
tm-of-code : Code → Opt ETm
tm-of-code (cvar v) = some (etv v)
tm-of-code (cglob g) = some (etc g)
tm-of-code (cann t T) = tm-of-code t
tm-of-code (capp f x) =
  case tm-of-code f of
    none → none
    some tf → (case tm-of-code x of none → none; some tx → some (eapp tf tx))
tm-of-code c = none
